<title>PAKISTAN: Shell Pakistan rises 2.53 percent.</title>
<headline>Shell Pakistan rises 2.53 percent.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Pakistan Ltd's 10-rupee stock rose seven rupees, or 2.53 percent, to 284 on Wednesday on the Karachi Stock Exchange on expectations of good corporate results for the year ended in June, dealers said.</p>
<p>About 4,000 shares changed hands in the morning trade, a dealer said. The company, with a listed paid-up capital of 233.77 million rupees ($5.77 million) on the Karachi Stock Exchange, announced an after-tax profit of 379 million rupees for the first half to December, compared to the year-ago net profit of 102 million. ($1 = 40.4 rupees) -- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
